<title>PAKISTAN: Pakistan auctions bonds worth 110.95 mln rupees.</title>
<headline>Pakistan auctions bonds worth 110.95 mln rupees.</headline>
<dateline>KARACHI, Pakistan 1997-01-13</dateline>
<text>
<p>The State (central) Bank of Pakistan said it had auctioned 10-year maturity federal investment bonds worth 110.9526 million rupees on Monday.</p>
<p>It said bids worth 110.9526 million rupees were accepted at par for the 10-year bonds. No bids were received for three-year and five-year bonds. The auction would be settled on Wednesday.</p>
<p>In the previous auction held on December 14, the bank accepted bids worth 12.3513 million rupees at a bid rate of 99.90 and above for 10-year maturity bonds.</p>
<p>-- Karachi newsroom 9221-5685192</p>
</text>
